s":"bamboo-like shoulders"},{"surface":"எல்வளை","parts":[{"text":"எல்","lemma":"el","gloss":"bright"},{"text":"வளை","lemma":"vaḷai","gloss":"bangles"}],"gloss":"bright bangles"},{"surface":"மகளிர்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"makaḷir","gloss":"women"}],"gloss":"women"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"துணங்கை","parts":[{"text":"துணங்கை","lemma":"tuṇaṅkai","gloss":"tuṇangai dance"}],"gloss":"tuṇangai dance"},{"surface":"நாளும்","parts":[{"text":"நாளும்","lemma":"nāḷum","gloss":"days"}],"gloss":"days"},{"surface":"வந்தன","parts":[{"text":"வந்தன","lemma":"vantana","gloss":"have come"}],"gloss":"have come"},{"surface":"அவ்வரைக்","parts":[{"text":"அவ்வரைக்","lemma":"அவ்வரைக்","gloss":"to that arena"}],"gloss":"to that arena","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கண்பொர","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eyes"},{"text":"பொர","lemma":"pora","gloss":"to clash"}],"gloss":"as eyes clash"},{"surface":"மற்றதன்","parts":[{"text":"மற்று","lemma":"maṟṟu","gloss":"then"},{"text":"அதன்","lemma":"ataṉ","gloss":"its"}],"gloss":"then in its"},{"surface":"கண்ணவர்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"place"},{"text":"அவர்","lemma":"avar","gloss":"they"}],"gloss":"place, they"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மணங்கொளற்","parts":[{"text":"மணங்கொளற்","lemma":"மணங்கொளற்","gloss":"to embrace"}],"gloss":"to embrace","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிவரும்","parts":[{"text":"கிவரும்","lemma":"கிவரும்","gloss":"who eagerly approach"}],"gloss":"who eagerly approach","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மள்ளர்","parts":[{"text":"மள்ளர்","lemma":"maḷḷar","gloss":"warriors"}],"gloss":"warriors"},{"surface":"போரே","parts":[{"text":"போர்","lemma":"pōr","gloss":"battle"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"like a battle"}]}],"literal":"Tangled creeper rattan-cane's striped-backed otter / scabbard-fish morning prey gets chief of the town / golden-stemmed shining bangles possessing her worthy wife / behind my back speaks, they say, clearly / curved wrists bamboo-like shoulders bright bangles women / tuṇangai dance days have come, to that arena / eyes clash, then in its place they / to embrace eagerly approach warriors like a battle.","translation":"The chief's town is where the striped-backed otter, hiding in the tangled creepers of rattan cane, catches the scabbard-fish for its morning prey. They say his worthy wife, who wears shining golden bangles, clearly speaks ill of me behind my back. Let her! The days of the Tuṇangai dance have arrived for the women with curved wrists, bamboo-like shoulders, and bright bangles. In that festival arena, where eyes clash, the young warriors will eagerly rush to embrace them, like a battle.","modern":"அடர்ந்த கொடிகளையுடைய பிரம்புப் புதரில் இருக்கும் வரிகளையுடைய முதுகைக் கொண்ட நீர்நாய், காலையில் வாளை மீனை இரையாகப் பெறும் நீர்நாட்டிற்குத் தலைவன் அவன். அவனுடைய தகுதியான மனைவி, பொன்னால் செய்த விளங்கும் வளையல்களை அணிந்தவள், என்னைப்பற்றிப் புறங்கூறுகிறாள் என்று தெளிவாகச் சொல்கிறார்கள். வளைந்த மணிக்கட்டுகளையும், மூங்கில் போன்ற தோள்களையும், விளங்கும் வளையல்களையும் உடைய மகளிர் ஆடும் துணங்கைக் கூத்துக்கான விழா நாட்கள் வந்துவிட்டன. அந்த விழா இடத்தில், கண்கள் ஒன்றோடொன்று மோத, பெண்களைத் தழுவிக்கொள்வதற்காக வீரர்கள் போரிடுவது போலப் போட்டியிட்டுக்கொண்டு வருவார்கள்.","explanation":"The speaker is the domestic courtesan (irparattai), reacting to the news that the chief's wife has been gossiping about her. She describes the chief's fertile agricultural town (marutam landscape) where an otter hiding in the rattan thicket catches a scabbard-fish for its morning prey. This image implies that the chief, though bound to his home, easily strays to seek pleasure elsewhere. The courtesan dismisses the wife's gossip, pointing out that the festival of the Tuṇangai dance has arrived. In this festival, women with beautiful shoulders and bright bangles dance, and young men eagerly compete to embrace them. She confidently implies that she will win the chief back at the festival, rendering the wife's complaints useless.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.5,2.0],[2.0,2.4],[2.4,2.8],[2.8,2.9],[2.9,3.7],[4.4,4.7],[4.7,5.44],[5.44,5.92],[5.92,6.4],[6.45,6.6],[6.65,6.8],[6.8,7.6],[7.6,8.0],[8.2,9.4],[9.4,9.9],[9.9,10.2],[10.2,10.6],[10.6,11.5],[11.5,11.6],[11.6,12.0],[12.2,12.81],[12.81,12.81],[12.81,14.1],[14.1,14.6],[14.6,15.23],[15.23,15.4],[15.4,16.36],[16.36,16.66]],"female":[[0.0,0.9],[0.9,1.3],[1.3,1.9],[1.9,2.4],[2.4,3.0],[3.0,3.5],[3.5,3.6],[3.6,4.3],[4.3,4.77],[4.77,4.77],[4.77,4.77],[4.77,4.77],[4.77,4.77],[4.77,5.0],[5.0,8.1],[8.1,8.6],[8.6,8.6],[8.6,10.7],[10.7,11.0],[11.0,11.4],[11.4,12.3],[12.3,12.4],[12.4,13.2],[13.2,13.91],[13.91,14.54],[14.54,14.86],[14.86,15.8],[15.8,16.42],[16.42,16.5],[16.5,17.62],[17.62,17.92]]},"sync":[[["அரில்","tangled"],["பவர்","creeper"]],[["பிரம்பின்","of the rattan cane"]],[["வரிப்புற","striped-backed"]],[["நீர்நாய்","otter"]],[["வாளை","scabbard-fish"]],[["நாளிரை","morning prey"]],[["பெறூஉம்","which obtains"]],[["ஊரன்","the chief of the town"]],[["பொற்கோல்","golden-stemmed"]],[["அவிர்தொடித்","shining bangles"]],[["தற்கெழு","possessing her"]],[["தகுவி","worthy wife"]],[["எற்புறங்","behind my back"]],[["கூறும்","speaks"]],[["என்ப","they say"]],[["தெற்றென","clearly"]],[["வணங்கிறைப்","curved wrists"]],[["பணைத்தோள்","bamboo-like shoulders"]],[["எல்வளை","bright bangles"]],[["மகளிர்","women"]],[["துணங்கை","tuṇangai dance"]],[["நாளும்","days"]],[["வந்தன","have come"]],[["அவ்வரைக்","to that arena"]],[["கண்பொர","as eyes clash"]],[["மற்றதன்","then in its"]],[["கண்ணவர்","place, they"]],[["மணங்கொளற்","to embrace"]],[["கிவரும்","who eagerly approach"]],[["மள்ளர்","warriors"]],[["போரே","like a battle"]]]}